## Audit status and limits

- Phase 3 Remoting inventory has no `NOT MAPPED` row after `ErrorSource`
  identity parity. The source-recorded Java `ChannelWrapper.reconnect()`
  `tryLock` race remains: deterministic coverage verifies post-swap retry but
  not every simultaneous lock-contention order. Rust's global connection-map
  mutex is not a faithful equivalent of Java's per-wrapper lock; no
  superficial locking change was made.
- The Phase 6 map still calls for complete method/overload,
  input/default/error/control-flow and reverse-export reconciliation across
  DTO, route, heartbeat, enum, configuration and subscription surfaces. Broad
  P18-V01 remains PARTIAL.
- P18-V03 local docs/provenance/package review is complete. P18-V02 local
  server-free gates pass on code revision `1e928372`. Native Windows runtime
  and current-revision remote Ubuntu CI remain unverified; P18-V04 remains
  open. Phase 19 Broker/Docker validation remains separate.
- No push or remote CI was run. The protected Phase 19 worktree files were
  not modified or staged.

