## P18-V01 `MessageExt` body-array alias continuation — 2026-10-24

- Code commit: `950cf356 fix(common): preserve subtype message body aliases`.
- Added `MessageExtSubtype::{shared_body,set_shared_body}` and
  `MessageExt::{shared_body,set_body_shared}`. Snapshot-only body overrides
  still work; custom subtype adapters can now retain and expose the shared
  mutable byte-array handle used by Java.
- Extended the pinned Java direct-consume fixture and Rust callback check to
  compare `setBody` input identity, caller mutation visibility, `getBody()`
  alias identity, getter-to-subtype mutation, and subtype-to-later-getter
  mutation. Fixture SHA-256:
  `4ba7bf76f4ef8ebb1ecc116f253d5b8e64100cf83096e65ff86958425f403b5c`.
- Focused gates passed: Common `message_decode` (28 tests), consumer
  `runtime_direct_consume` (6 tests), and Java fixture `--verify` (29 direct
  cases).
- On `950cf356`, default and all-feature locked workspace test/doctest runs
  each passed 93 suites and 2,019 tests. Strict all-target/all-feature
  workspace Clippy passed. Release workspace examples built. Windows GNU
  all-target/all-feature workspace check and strict Clippy passed as
  compile-only gates. Offline Maven `verify` passed: 37 scenarios, 11 message
  fixtures, 106 typed headers, 19 typed bodies, including the updated direct
  consumer fixture.
- The first default workspace test launch in the repository target stalled
  before Rust test code in the macOS dynamic loader for the Remoting `codec`
